  {
    "date": "2022-05-19",
    "term": "挟む",
    "kana": "はさむ",
    "meaning": "to pinch; to hold between; to insert",
    "level": "N2",
    "pos": ["Godan verb with 'mu' ending", "transitive verb"],
    "priority": ["ichi1", "news1", "nf24"],
    "stratum": "wago",
    "processes": ["compound", "derivation"],
    "headline": "挟む appears to be the Old Japanese root pasa plus the verb-forming suffix む (mu).",
    "morphemes": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "Likely from Old Japanese. First attested in isolation with unambiguous phonetics in 950. Also attested in compound verb sashihasamu in the Kojiki of 712, but the relevant section of text is written in kundoku (a kind of written Classical Chinese read out in Japanese) in the ideographic spelling 刺挟, and the phonetic realization as Japanese is not clearly attested until later."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Derivationally, this appears to be Old Japanese root pasa (modern hasa) + verb-forming suffix む (mu, “seem like, look like; treat like; make like”). Root pasa may be a kind of ablaut cognate with poso as reflected in modern adjective 細い (hosoi, “narrow”), and adverbs 細々 (hosoboso, “narrowly”, iterative, repetitive), ほっそり (hossori, “narrowly, skinnily”, stative). Root pasa is also reflected in modern noun 稲架 (hasa, “frame for drying sheaves of harvested rice”)."
      }
    ],
    "examples": [
      {
        "id": 105247,
        "ja": "彼は耳に鉛筆を挟んだ。",
        "en": "He stuck his pencil behind his ear.",
        "enId": 298442,
        "form": "挟んだ"
      },
      {
        "id": 159386,
        "ja": "ドアに指をはさまれた。",
        "en": "I had my fingers caught in the door.",
        "enId": 255137,
        "form": "はさまれた"
      }
    ],
    "wiktionaryDump": "2026-09-02"
